    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-context.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The fields — read them off the schema, never off this page",
      "prov:value": "`SessionContextSchema` in `schemas/sdlc/session-context.ts` is authoritative. This\ndescription said *\"the six fields\"* until 2026-09-24, by which point there were\n**eight** — `waitingOn` and `$schema` had joined `id`, `actor`, `startedAt`,\n`updatedAt`, `open`, `claimed`. Bean `s8mo` carried the same \"six\" and drifted\nwith it, so the bean and this skill agreed with each other and both disagreed\nwith the code, which is the one shape comparing them cannot catch.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean s8mo",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-context.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Who reads it, and why it is parsed rather than trusted",
      "prov:value": "The writer may be an LLM playing the part of a state machine (bean `3nfv`), so\nthe shape cannot be assumed from the writer's care. `parseSessionContext()`\nparses at the boundary, which is what makes a **non-deterministic writer safe\nto read from** — and that is the general rule this record is the first case of:\nwhere a machine may be played rather than executed, the schema is the contract\nand the parse is where it is enforced.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3nfv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-context.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this is NOT",
      "prov:value": "**Not a store yet.** The kind is registered and the shape is defined; nothing\nwrites one. The state machine is bean `3nfv`, and declaring a directory before\nanything fills it is the defect where a consumer scans nothing and reports a\nclean run.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3nfv"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
